    content: {
      intro:
        "A 4-day, 3-night trip from Lahore to Dubai costs roughly PKR 2.4 to 3.2 lakh per person in October 2026 on a budget-to-mid-range plan, before shopping. That covers a return flight (from about PKR 1.3–1.5 lakh), a 30-day tourist visa (AED 200 government fee, about PKR 16,000 with VAT), three nights in a budget or 3-star hotel, Burj Khalifa, an evening desert safari, metro travel and simple meals. Flights and hotels are the biggest costs and change the most, so booking early and travelling outside peak season (November to April) saves the most. Prices below use 1 AED ≈ PKR 77.",
      sections: [
        {
          heading: "Key facts at a glance",
          subsections: [
            {
              title: "4-day Dubai trip from Lahore (Oct 2026)",
              items: [
                "Total per person: about PKR 2.4–3.2 lakh, budget to mid-range, before shopping.",
                "Exchange rate used: 1 AED ≈ PKR 77 (interbank was PKR 76.50 on 9 October 2026).",
                "Return flight Lahore–Dubai: from about PKR 1.3–1.5 lakh in economy.",
                "30-day tourist visa: AED 200 government fee plus VAT; agency packages cost more.",
                "Budget/3-star hotel: about AED 150–350 a night, plus a Tourism Dirham fee of AED 7–20 a night.",
                "Burj Khalifa (levels 124/125): from AED 161 for adults.",
                "Evening desert safari with BBQ: about AED 210–253 per person.",
                "Dubai Metro: AED 20 day pass on a Silver nol card (card AED 25).",
              ],
            },
          ],
        },
        {
          heading: "1. Flights from Lahore to Dubai",
          content:
            "Lahore to Dubai is about a three-hour flight with several direct options. On 9 October 2026, one-way economy fares for the next day started at about PKR 69,000 on AirSial, Airblue and PIA, and about PKR 1.1 lakh on Emirates and Qatar Airways ([Sastaticket](https://www.sastaticket.pk/flights/cheap-flights-from-lahore-to-dubai)). A return trip on a budget carrier therefore starts at roughly PKR 1.3–1.5 lakh, and more on full-service airlines or in December and Eid holidays.",
          subsections: [
            {
              title: "Save on flights",
              items: [
                "Book 4–8 weeks ahead and compare AirSial, Airblue, PIA, flydubai and Air Arabia.",
                "Check the baggage allowance before comparing prices; the cheapest fares often include less.",
                "Avoid December, Eid and school holidays if your dates are flexible.",
                "Your return ticket is also needed for the visa and at airport check-in.",
              ],
            },
          ],
        },
        {
          heading: "2. Dubai visit visa cost from Pakistan",
          content:
            "A 30-day single-entry tourist visa has a government fee of AED 200, or AED 300 for 60 days, plus 5% VAT, and must be filed through an accredited tourism office ([GDRFA Dubai](https://gdrfad.gov.ae/en/node/13896)). At 1 AED ≈ PKR 77, AED 210 is about PKR 16,000. Agencies add their service charge and usually include health insurance, so the price you pay in Pakistan is higher. Many agencies also ask for a bank statement: see [how much bank balance you need](/blog/dubai-visit-visa-bank-statement-pakistan).",
        },
        {
          heading: "3. Hotels for 3 nights",
          content:
            "Budget hotels in Deira, Bur Dubai and Al Barsha are typically around AED 150–350 a night, and mid-range 3–4 star hotels around AED 300–600 ([Two Continents](https://twocontinents.com/blog/hotels-in-dubai-cost)). Prices rise from November to April and fall in the summer. Every hotel also adds a Tourism Dirham fee per room per night: AED 7 for budget hotels and guest houses, AED 10 for 3-star, AED 15 for 4-star and AED 20 for 5-star ([Arabian Business](https://www.arabianbusiness.com/industries/travel-hospitality/guide-dubai-s-tourism-dirham-scheme-544516)). For three nights, budget roughly AED 470–1,080 (PKR 36,000–83,000) per room. Two people sharing a room halves this per person.",
          note:
            "Staying near a metro station in Deira or Bur Dubai keeps both hotel and transport costs down, and these areas have plenty of Pakistani and Indian restaurants.",
        },
        {
          heading: "4. Burj Khalifa and the desert safari",
          content:
            "These are the two activities most Pakistani families book. At the Top, Burj Khalifa (levels 124 and 125) starts from AED 161 for adults and AED 127 for children aged 3 to 8; sunset slots cost more ([Platinumlist](https://dubai.platinumlist.net/event-tickets/73366/at-the-top-burj-khalifa)). A standard shared evening desert safari with dune driving, BBQ dinner and shows costs about AED 210–253 per person, and premium options with quad biking about AED 420–499 ([The Better Vacation](https://thebettervacation.com/price-of-desert-safari-dubai)). Free sights such as the Dubai Fountain, Dubai Mall, JBR beach and the Creek abra area fill the rest of the days cheaply.",
        },
        {
          heading: "5. Getting around Dubai",
          content:
            "The Dubai Metro is the cheapest way to get around. A Silver nol card costs AED 25 including AED 19 credit, single trips cost AED 3–7.50 depending on zones, and a Silver day pass is AED 20 for unlimited travel ([Property Finder](https://www.propertyfinder.ae/blog/dubai-metro-fare-calculator/)). For four days, about AED 80–100 (PKR 6,000–8,000) per person covers metro travel, with taxis or ride-hailing for the safari pickup if it isn't included.",
        },
        {
          heading: "6. Food, SIM and small costs",
          content:
            "There's no official figure for food, but Pakistani and Indian restaurants in Deira, Bur Dubai and Karama keep meals affordable. As a rough planning allowance, budget about AED 60–100 a day per person (PKR 4,600–7,700) for simple meals and water; eating in malls costs more. For data, compare your Pakistani network's roaming bundle with a UAE tourist SIM before you fly. Keep some cash for small purchases: travellers have also been asked at airports to show funds of about AED 3,000 in cash or on a card ([Khaleej Times](https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/dubai-visit-visa-holders-told-to-carry-dh3000-in-cash-or-credit-return-tickets-proof-of-stay)).",
        },
